load_default_library collects each lookup's NS::Error in `error[6]` and reads all six to build its
"Failed to load the default metallib" message, but `error[5]` is only written under SWIFTPM_BUNDLE.
Without it the read is of an uninitialized pointer: AppleClang 21 at -O3 compiles that path to a
trap, so a missing mlx.metallib kills the process (SIGTRAP in metal::Device::Device) instead of
throwing the std::runtime_error mlx-c turns into an error return.

Applied by scripts/build-mlx-static.sh only (libPicoMlxServe.dylib must fail a call, not its host).
Retires when MLX initializes the array. Not reported upstream yet.

diff --git a/mlx/backend/metal/device.cpp b/mlx/backend/metal/device.cpp
index 6c0c92f..5142fd4 100644
--- a/mlx/backend/metal/device.cpp
+++ b/mlx/backend/metal/device.cpp
@@ -223,7 +223,7 @@ MTL::Library* load_default_library(MTL::Device* device) {
     return lib;
   }
 
-  NS::Error* error[6];
+  NS::Error* error[6] = {};
   MTL::Library* lib;
   // First try the colocated mlx.metallib
   std::tie(lib, error[0]) = load_colocated_library(device, "mlx");
